error.description:
## Active document does not match the current AYON context
{msg}
**AYON context:** {folder_path} / {task_name}
**Expected work root:** {expected_work_root}
**Active document directory:** {current_dir}
### Why does this happen?
When you open a Photoshop document directly (not through the AYON Workfiles tool), the AYON session context is not updated. If you then publish, outputs would be filed under the wrong folder or task.
### How to fix?
{repair_msg}
If you changed context via the Workfiles tool but are still seeing this error, close and reopen the correct workfile from Workfiles to refresh the session context.
(Context = combination of project, folder path and task name.)

## The active document changed after the publisher was opened or refreshed

    {msg}

**Previously active document:** {previous_doc_name}

**Currently active document:** {doc_name}

### Why does this happen?

Photoshop can have multiple documents open at once. AYON automatically
keeps its session context in sync with whichever document is active, but
the instances and report you see in the publisher were collected for the
document that was active when it was last opened or refreshed.

### How to fix?

    {repair_msg}
